  {
    "id": "work-1772351126342-g3bhxx",
    "slug": "honkai-star-rail-character-shader-study-breakdown-rebuild",
    "category": "shader",
    "title_en": "Honkai: Star Rail — Character Shader Study (Breakdown + Rebuild)",
    "title_zh": "崩坏：星穹铁道 - 角色渲染方案拆解复刻",
    "summary_en": "A systematic breakdown and rebuild of the Honkai: Star Rail character rendering approach—from material layering and lighting response to face/hair treatment, outlines, and stylized post effects. Reproduced the core visual logic and distilled transferable shader implementation and performance optimization takeaways for UE/Unity.",
    "summary_zh": "对《崩坏：星穹铁道》角色渲染进行系统拆解与重建：从材质分层、光照响应、脸部/头发处理到描边与后期风格化，复现核心视觉逻辑，并总结可迁移到 UE/Unity 的 Shader 实现与性能优化要点。",
    "cover": "/works-media/works/draft/1772351116173-h1ihnh.png",
    "tags": [
      "UE5",
      "HLSL",
      "Shader"
    ],
    "year": 2024,
    "sort_order": 0,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "b-1772351102559-k0r2",
        "alt": "封面.png",
        "src": "/works-media/works/draft/1772351116173-h1ihnh.png",
        "type": "Image",
        "width": "full",
        "caption": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772371807799-jo8p",
        "alt": "大图.png",
        "src": "/works-media/works/work-1772351126342-g3bhxx/1772371814475-kkvp8t.png",
        "type": "Image",
        "width": "full",
        "caption": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772376886093-l7bv",
        "src": "/works-media/works/work-1772351126342-g3bhxx/videos/1772377432289-58uvpo.mp4",
        "type": "Video",
        "width": "full",
        "poster": "",
        "caption": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772373722705-7wzz",
        "type": "Title",
        "width": "full",
        "content": "Face SDF",
        "content_zh": "面部 SDF"
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772373697261-z693",
        "alt": "1.png",
        "src": "/works-media/works/work-1772351126342-g3bhxx/1772373709696-p387iv.png",
        "type": "Image",
        "width": "full",
        "caption": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772372002932-cwf3",
        "alt": "SDF.png",
        "src": "/works-media/works/work-1772351126342-g3bhxx/1772372007713-o35etp.png",
        "type": "Image",
        "width": "full",
        "caption": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772373738277-72p2",
        "type": "Text",
        "align": "left",
        "width": "full",
        "content": "To render the face, SDF (Signed Distance Field) is used. First, the forward, right, and up vectors of the head are obtained. The light vector is then adjusted to the horizontal plane of the head's coordinate system using the up vector. By performing a dot product between the new light vector and the right vector, the light's position relative to the face (left or right) is determined. Based on this, the UV horizontal coordinate of the SDF is adjusted to sample the corresponding grayscale value. To avoid incorrect rendering when the light is centered, a slight offset is applied to the sampling position. Finally, a threshold is obtained by taking the dot product of the light vector and the forward vector, and smoothstep is used for smooth comparison. Lerp interpolation is then applied to replace areas not affected by SDF with ambient occlusion (AO).",
        "content_zh": "制作脸部渲染，使用了SDF技术。首先，获取头部的前向量、右向量和上向量。通过上向量将光照方向调整至头部坐标系的水平面，并利用新光向量与右向量的点积来判断光线在脸部的左右位置。接着，基于这一判断调整SDF的UV横坐标，从而获取对应的灰度值。在光照位于中心时，稍微偏移采样位置以避免错误的渲染。最后，通过点乘前向量与光向量得到一个阈值，并使用smoothstep进行平滑比较，再通过Lerp进行插值，将不受SDF影响的区域用AO替代。"
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772374195467-53cm",
        "type": "Title",
        "width": "full",
        "content": "Black Stockings",
        "content_zh": "黑丝"
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772374244609-j0c5",
        "alt": "HighresScreenshot00005.png",
        "src": "/works-media/works/work-1772351126342-g3bhxx/1772374251723-9tzynl.png",
        "type": "Image",
        "width": "half",
        "caption": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772374259207-tn1t",
        "alt": "SilkStockings.png",
        "src": "/works-media/works/work-1772351126342-g3bhxx/1772374262673-3tbk6l.png",
        "type": "Image",
        "width": "half",
        "caption": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "b-1772374270438-s8og",
        "type": "Text",
        "align": "left",
        "width": "full",
        "content": "The stocking shader is built from two key components: view-dependent translucency/specular response and fabric pattern detail.\nFirst, a Fresnel term is used to drive the view-angle response, producing the characteristic change in appearance across viewing angles (subtler when facing the camera and stronger at grazing angles), which helps simulate the lighting and see-through feel of stockings. This Fresnel result is then blended with the stocking’s fabric texture to establish the base structure and micro detail.\n\nFor art-directable tone and color variation, the shader also samples a gradient ramp. In Unreal Engine, this is authored as a Curve and registered into a Curve Atlas, allowing the material to sample it like a texture. Finally, the ramp output is combined with the Fresnel/texture layers to achieve the final stocking look.",
        "content_zh": "黑丝效果主要分两部分：视角相关的透光/高光与织物纹理。\n首先使用 Fresnel（菲涅尔） 构建视角响应：让材质在不同观察角度下产生变化（更贴近视线时更透/更弱，掠射角更明显），用来模拟黑丝随角度变化的光照与通透感。随后将该 Fresnel 结果与黑丝的织物纹理进行混合，形成基础的结构与细节。\n\n为了控制颜色与明暗层次，黑丝额外采样一条颜色渐变（Gradient Ramp）。在 Unreal Engine 中可以用 Curve（曲线） 来制作这条渐变，将曲线注册到 Curve Atlas（曲线图谱） 后，即可在材质中作为纹理进行采样。最终将渐变结果与 Fresnel/纹理混合，完成黑丝的整体表现。"
      }
    ],
    "createdAt": "2026-03-01T07:45:25.273+00:00",
    "updatedAt": "2026-03-01T15:05:43.908+00:00"
  },
  {
